title:: BMAbstractGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - abstract superclass of all GUI classes in the BEASTmulch library
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMAbstractGUI is the abstract superclass of all GUI classes in the BEASTmulch library. It implements a few inherited methods and defines an interface.

You can see a list of all available subclasses by executing the following:

code::
BMAbstractGUI.dumpClassSubtree;
::

Their help files and source code provide many useful examples.

See also: link::Classes/Window::, link::Classes/View::

INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: name
The name displayed in the title bar of this object's link::Classes/Window:: as a link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol::. Usually this corresponds to the name of the object it represents.
				
method:: window
Returns this object's link::Classes/Window::.
				
				
method:: onClose
Register a link::Classes/Function:: to be executed when this object's window is closed.
		
argument:: func
An instance of link::Classes/Function::. It will be passed the receiver as an argument.


method:: makeWindow
Subclasses should override this as needed to create a link::Classes/Window::.


method:: close
Close this object's window and call any function registered in strong::onClose::.
